# Scanner laws (full brief: AGENTS.md)

- One multiformat scan engine, one package family: QR Code & Barcode Scanner.
  Source: `qrcode-ai-com/qrcode-barcode-scanner`; existing install names retain
  `qrcode-ai-scanner`. No QR/barcode engine extraction or alias/wrapper packages.
  QR Code AI and its creation engine have separate release processes; a scanner
  binding is not an app. See SOURCE-AND-EXTRACTION.md. Preserve dated receipts
  and component licenses.
- Existing public package contracts: the `ScanReport` wire is
  additive-only forever; score semantic changes bump `score_contract`;
  public enums stay `#[non_exhaustive]`.
- No supported code found is `Ok` with empty detections — `Err` = `QRS-001..005`
  only (stable registry, never reused).
- Determinism follows AGENTS.md/spec: unbounded attempts are reproducible,
  with the documented upstream PDF417 confidence-tie exception. Introduce no
  hidden RNG or wall-clock dependency; time-budget cuts retain their flags.
- Zero `unwrap`/`expect`/`panic!` in production (lint-denied); engine
  panics degrade to no-score at the boundary, never a crash.
- Decoded text is attacker-controlled — strip terminal controls on any
  human echo; colour only via the CLI's term.rs seam.
- Gates: use RELEASING.md's Local development checks with its exact compiler
  selector, `--locked`, formatting check, tests/doc tests, strict Clippy,
  type parity and separately tested MSRV. Core/dependency changes affect
  root plus Python, UniFFI, Flutter Rust and fuzz lock roots. Workspace
  tests and locked metadata do not replace installed artifact consumers.
- Release qualification follows RELEASING.md: source/version synchronization,
  exact artifacts, applicable consumers, CI and publisher admission before tag.
  Downstream repos pin this version as
  "the judge" — score honesty is a contract.
- Commits: `type(scope): lowercase` + `Co-Authored-By: Nika 🦋
  <nika@supernovae.studio>`.
